## Important Domain Concepts

### Pattern-Based Dynamic Sessions
Routine templates and muscle-group slots are RETIRED. A session is built live:
- **Day Plan**: carries pattern goals (target sets per movement pattern), not an exercise list
- **Movement Pattern**: every exercise maps to one of ten curated patterns
- **Superset Round**: an anchor plus a partner working the OPPOSITE pattern, drawn from the user's staple pool
- **Proposal**: starting a session proposes a whole workout, which the user adjusts by swapping slots
See @CLAUDE.md "Pattern-Based Dynamic Sessions" for the full rules.

### Exercise Variants
- Users can duplicate exercises to create variants (HIIT vs Strength)
- Each variant tracks its own history and PRs
- Linked via `base_exercise_id`

### Equipment Profiles
- Location-based equipment presets (Home Gym, Work Gym, etc.)
- Applied at workout start to filter available exercises
- Can override per-slot

## FastAPI Server Management (CRITICAL)

**Stale server processes cause new endpoints to not appear in OpenAPI/Swagger.**

### Before ANY Backend Testing
Use the restart script (preferred) or manual commands:

```bash
# PREFERRED: Run from project root
.\restart-server.bat

# OR manual commands:
taskkill /F /IM python.exe 2>$null; taskkill /F /IM uvicorn.exe 2>$null
cd backend
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
```

### Symptoms of Stale Server (STOP and restart if you see these)
- New endpoints missing from http://localhost:8000/docs
- OpenAPI schema doesn't reflect code changes
- API returns 404 for newly added endpoints
- Changes to Pydantic schemas not reflected

### Required Workflow for Backend Changes
1. Make code changes
2. **Kill ALL Python processes** (taskkill command above)
3. Start server fresh
4. Verify in Swagger UI before proceeding
5. Do NOT assume --reload caught the changes

**Never skip the kill step when debugging "missing endpoint" issues.**

## Common Commands

```bash
# Backend - Use restart script (kills stale processes automatically)
.\restart-server.bat
alembic upgrade head
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "description"
pytest

# Web
cd web
npm install
npm run dev
npm run build
```

## Do's and Don'ts

### Do
- Reference existing code patterns before creating new ones
- Run migrations after model changes
- Add type hints to all new code
- Update the active plan in @docs/superpowers/plans/ when completing tasks
- Test API changes at http://localhost:8000/docs

### Don't
- Modify the exercise CSV in `assets/`
- Skip Alembic migrations for schema changes
- Use `any` type in TypeScript
- Create new CSS files (use Tailwind)
- Add authentication yet (deferred for MVP)
